1
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:09,520
Ramil.

2
00:03:09,600 --> 00:03:10,440
PREVIOUSLY

3
00:03:10,520 --> 00:03:12,920
You and I are both
supervisors now. Same level.

4
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:15,840
We're not friends.
Don't act familiar with me.

5
00:03:15,920 --> 00:03:19,680
Boss, that guy looks like trouble.
Want us to handle it?

6
00:03:19,760 --> 00:03:23,240
And from now on,
you're going to stop seeing Chayanee.

7
00:03:23,320 --> 00:03:28,680
I certainly didn't want to set foot
in this shabby house of a man I rejected.

8
00:03:29,680 --> 00:03:32,040
-You rejected Chayanee?
-Yes.

9
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:36,240
If you didn't do it,
why don't you clear your name?

10
00:03:36,320 --> 00:03:39,240
I only tell the truth
to people I really care about.

11
00:03:51,720 --> 00:03:53,160
Try it.

12
00:03:53,920 --> 00:03:55,360
You try it too.

13
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:05,560
Well?

14
00:04:06,920 --> 00:04:07,760
Is it good?

15
00:04:10,440 --> 00:04:11,680
It's pretty good.

16
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:17,519
See? I told you I could be a chef.

17
00:04:20,480 --> 00:04:25,080
I think you're better off
supervising the construction site.

18
00:04:25,960 --> 00:04:30,360
-Don't go ruining MasterChef.
-Hey!

19
00:04:38,160 --> 00:04:40,440
Where's Max?

20
00:04:42,080 --> 00:04:42,920
Max.

21
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:45,000
Tonight you're staying
at your friend's house again.

22
00:04:45,080 --> 00:04:46,960
Again?

23
00:04:47,040 --> 00:04:50,560
Every time I stay at my friend's place,
I have to bring them something.

24
00:04:53,360 --> 00:04:54,920
Thank you, boss.

25
00:04:57,160 --> 00:05:01,880
Why has Max been staying
at his friend's place so often lately?

26
00:05:05,400 --> 00:05:06,720
Well…

27
00:05:06,800 --> 00:05:09,520
Max's friend just got his heart broken.

28
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:13,760
Max is worried he might do something
drastic, so he's keeping him company.

29
00:05:27,400 --> 00:05:29,880
I don't really like it.

30
00:05:30,840 --> 00:05:33,800
It'd be a waste. You eat it.

31
00:05:46,040 --> 00:05:46,880
Thanks.

32
00:05:48,280 --> 00:05:52,440
You don't have to thank me.
I just didn't want it to go to waste.

33
00:06:04,520 --> 00:06:07,320
So, tomorrow…

34
00:06:09,560 --> 00:06:14,560
I happen to be free.
Do you want to go somewhere?

35
00:06:14,640 --> 00:06:17,400
I'll take you.

36
00:06:18,720 --> 00:06:21,880
Anywhere is fine with me. I'm easygoing.

37
00:06:21,960 --> 00:06:26,480
Really? Then how about a boat ride
on the Chao Phraya River?

38
00:06:26,560 --> 00:06:29,640
Then we can visit a temple
and find a nice café afterward.

39
00:06:31,360 --> 00:06:34,880
Yes! Really?
That sounds great. I love that.

40
00:06:59,360 --> 00:07:01,720
On the night of the party,
did any outsiders come in?

41
00:07:01,800 --> 00:07:02,720
No, sir.

42
00:07:02,800 --> 00:07:06,600
It was only us helping set everything up
and welcoming the guests.

43
00:07:06,680 --> 00:07:09,080
-Nothing left to do here. Go take a break.
-Okay.

44
00:07:10,480 --> 00:07:12,080
Pong was there that night.

45
00:07:13,920 --> 00:07:18,560
Pong helped carry some things, but I
didn't let him wander around the party.

46
00:07:19,400 --> 00:07:22,080
Why are you asking about this, sir?
Is something wrong?

47
00:07:23,120 --> 00:07:26,320
No. Go back to work.

48
00:07:28,440 --> 00:07:32,520
Master, I raised Miss Hathaya
from the time she was little.

49
00:07:33,600 --> 00:07:37,800
I'm certain she isn't that kind of person.

50
00:07:38,560 --> 00:07:42,280
Even though she grew up with Hathai,

51
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:46,360
from the time I've spent with Miss Hathaya
and the conversations we've had,

52
00:07:46,440 --> 00:07:50,960
I truly believe she is
nothing like Hathai.

53
00:08:02,560 --> 00:08:04,080
Is there anything you need, sir?

54
00:08:08,400 --> 00:08:09,320
No.

55
00:08:10,200 --> 00:08:14,520
I was just passing by and thought
I'd check whether you needed anything.

56
00:08:15,280 --> 00:08:18,200
Not at all, sir.
Madam takes very good care of me.

57
00:08:18,920 --> 00:08:22,360
I thought you came all this way because
you needed my help at the main house.

58
00:08:22,440 --> 00:08:26,800
No need. There are plenty of people
there to take care of me.

59
00:08:27,400 --> 00:08:30,880
You stay where you belong.
No need for you to go anywhere else.

60
00:08:32,080 --> 00:08:32,919
Yes, sir.

61
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:51,520
Madam.

62
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:09,920
Pong? Pong, where are you?

63
00:09:22,120 --> 00:09:25,520
I'm sorry. I was taking a shower.

64
00:09:27,520 --> 00:09:31,080
Why did you call me all the way over here?

65
00:09:31,760 --> 00:09:34,000
Mr. Pichai came to see me this evening.

66
00:09:34,080 --> 00:09:36,480
He told me not to go
near the main house anymore.

67
00:09:37,840 --> 00:09:40,560
I think he suspects me of something.

68
00:09:42,200 --> 00:09:46,960
Why would Father suddenly suspect you?
Did you give him a reason to distrust you?

69
00:09:48,080 --> 00:09:49,200
I don't know either.

70
00:09:49,920 --> 00:09:54,440
Or did Ann tell him something?
Whatever happens, don't let anything slip.

71
00:10:04,920 --> 00:10:05,880
Yes.

72
00:10:08,920 --> 00:10:12,640
Next time, if it's something this minor,
just call me.

73
00:10:12,720 --> 00:10:14,680
You don't need to make me
come all the way here.

74
00:10:17,440 --> 00:10:18,600
Understood.

75
00:10:42,080 --> 00:10:44,440
Ramil, I'm ready!

76
00:10:49,440 --> 00:10:50,680
Hello?

77
00:10:53,200 --> 00:10:54,720
You're outside?

78
00:10:55,800 --> 00:10:58,440
You went out to get something?

79
00:10:58,520 --> 00:11:02,960
Okay. I'm ready.
I'll wait for you at home.

80
00:11:03,560 --> 00:11:04,600
Okay.

81
00:11:56,560 --> 00:11:59,360
Excuse me. Who are you?

82
00:12:00,320 --> 00:12:01,880
I'm here to see Ramil.

83
00:12:03,960 --> 00:12:07,000
Ramil went out to buy something.
He will be back soon.

84
00:12:07,920 --> 00:12:10,840
Are you a friend of Ramil's?

85
00:12:12,400 --> 00:12:13,600
Mom isn't his friend.

86
00:12:19,720 --> 00:12:21,280
Hello, handsome.

87
00:12:21,920 --> 00:12:27,080
If you're not his friend, then you
must be relatives of Ramil's, right?

88
00:12:27,160 --> 00:12:29,040
My son and I aren't Ramil's relatives.

89
00:12:33,720 --> 00:12:37,040
I'm sorry. What is your relationship
with Ramil?

90
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:44,120
I'm back. Let's go.

91
00:12:44,800 --> 00:12:46,040
Daddy!

92
00:12:47,040 --> 00:12:48,440
Papang!

93
00:12:56,720 --> 00:12:58,960
Let's sit down.

94
00:13:03,880 --> 00:13:06,560
I missed you more than anything, Dad.

95
00:13:07,200 --> 00:13:09,040
I missed you too. Come give me a kiss.

96
00:13:12,440 --> 00:13:14,640
Mommy missed you a lot too.

97
00:13:14,720 --> 00:13:17,080
Daddy, kiss Mommy on the cheek too.

98
00:13:36,200 --> 00:13:37,880
I should go.

99
00:13:37,960 --> 00:13:39,400
Wait.

100
00:13:42,280 --> 00:13:46,960
Uh… This is Nuchwara.

101
00:13:48,080 --> 00:13:50,240
She's my wife.

102
00:13:52,640 --> 00:13:54,120
Hello.

103
00:13:54,720 --> 00:13:58,320
And this is Papang.

104
00:13:59,440 --> 00:14:01,400
My son.

105
00:14:02,640 --> 00:14:08,040
Daddy, who is that auntie?
Why is she staying in your house?

106
00:14:10,680 --> 00:14:12,200
Well…

107
00:14:15,440 --> 00:14:16,760
She's…

108
00:14:16,840 --> 00:14:18,720
Is she your new maid?

109
00:14:23,600 --> 00:14:25,520
Uh… No…

110
00:14:25,600 --> 00:14:26,800
Yes.

111
00:14:27,920 --> 00:14:31,720
I'm the maid. I'm here to help
take care of your daddy's house.

112
00:14:34,400 --> 00:14:38,160
Have you finished your work?
If you're done, you can go home now.

113
00:14:40,520 --> 00:14:43,800
Auntie, don't come back.

114
00:14:43,880 --> 00:14:47,040
I want to stay with Daddy and Mommy. Shoo!

115
00:14:49,080 --> 00:14:50,280
Papang,

116
00:14:50,360 --> 00:14:53,440
don't talk like that. That's not nice.

117
00:14:53,520 --> 00:14:54,800
Okay, Daddy.

118
00:14:57,160 --> 00:14:58,600
I'll excuse myself.

119
00:15:14,760 --> 00:15:17,120
Ramil has a wife and a child.

120
00:15:17,920 --> 00:15:20,560
Why didn't anyone ever tell me?

121
00:15:32,640 --> 00:15:33,480
Hey.

122
00:15:33,560 --> 00:15:36,680
Why did you bring our son here?
Why didn't you tell me first?

123
00:15:38,520 --> 00:15:41,120
He was crying, so I brought him.

124
00:15:41,760 --> 00:15:42,960
Can't he miss his dad?

125
00:15:43,560 --> 00:15:46,840
But you know I have work.
I have other things to do too.

126
00:15:46,920 --> 00:15:50,440
Do those other things include
that woman from earlier?

127
00:15:51,560 --> 00:15:55,200
I'm not stupid. I know she isn't a maid.

128
00:15:55,280 --> 00:15:59,320
Then why did you tell Papang she was?

129
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:02,640
I just didn't want our son
thinking you have a new wife.

130
00:16:02,720 --> 00:16:05,680
I don't care who that woman is.

131
00:16:06,280 --> 00:16:08,640
But you are not allowed to hurt my son.

132
00:16:09,240 --> 00:16:12,560
I think Papang is old enough
to understand things now.

133
00:16:13,840 --> 00:16:15,480
Isn't it better to tell him the truth?

134
00:16:16,400 --> 00:16:18,680
If you want to hurt him,

135
00:16:18,760 --> 00:16:21,960
I can go tell him right now
that the two of us don't love each other,

136
00:16:22,040 --> 00:16:24,000
and then Papang will never
come back here again.

137
00:16:25,080 --> 00:16:26,120
Wait.

138
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:29,960
When the time comes,

139
00:16:30,880 --> 00:16:32,080
I'll tell him myself.

140
00:16:33,600 --> 00:16:34,680
As for you,

141
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:37,120
why did you come here?

142
00:16:37,720 --> 00:16:41,880
I have some business out of town,
so I wanted to leave Papang with you.

143
00:16:42,480 --> 00:16:43,440
When will you be back?

144
00:16:43,520 --> 00:16:46,560
It won't be long. About two days.

145
00:16:46,640 --> 00:16:48,560
As soon as I'm done, I'll hurry back.

146
00:16:59,520 --> 00:17:00,680
What are you thinking about?

147
00:17:09,760 --> 00:17:13,440
Come on. We live in the same compound.
There's no need to avoid me.

148
00:17:14,839 --> 00:17:15,800
Papang.

149
00:17:17,240 --> 00:17:18,079
Let me sit with you.

150
00:17:18,160 --> 00:17:20,640
Papang.

151
00:17:20,720 --> 00:17:24,000
Mommy has to go to work now.
Stay with Daddy, okay?

152
00:17:24,599 --> 00:17:28,480
I don't want Mommy to go.
Mommy, don't leave me.

153
00:17:33,080 --> 00:17:34,160
Papang,

154
00:17:34,680 --> 00:17:37,760
Mommy isn't leaving you.

155
00:17:37,840 --> 00:17:39,080
She just has to go to work.

156
00:17:39,600 --> 00:17:40,840
That's right.

157
00:17:40,920 --> 00:17:44,840
Mommy promises I'll come back
for you as soon as possible.

158
00:17:45,600 --> 00:17:47,560
Stay with Daddy for now, okay?

159
00:17:47,640 --> 00:17:49,560
Okay.

160
00:17:49,640 --> 00:17:51,200
Okay.

161
00:17:51,280 --> 00:17:52,920
-Now he's okay.
-Take care of him.

162
00:18:09,360 --> 00:18:11,440
Is something bothering you?

163
00:18:11,520 --> 00:18:13,960
No. I just wanted to come out
and get some fresh air.

164
00:18:15,080 --> 00:18:18,880
It's your day off. Ramil should've taken
his girlfriend out to eat or go shopping.

165
00:18:53,080 --> 00:18:53,920
Nuch.

166
00:18:55,520 --> 00:18:57,040
You know her too?

167
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:04,160
Nuchwara is Ramil's wife.

168
00:19:06,680 --> 00:19:08,400
I never knew anything about this.

169
00:19:10,840 --> 00:19:14,520
Honestly, no one really wants
to talk about it. I don't want to either.

170
00:19:15,920 --> 00:19:18,280
There are some beautiful flowers

171
00:19:18,360 --> 00:19:20,360
over in that park.
I can take you to see them.

172
00:19:21,080 --> 00:19:24,040
No, thank you. Nuch has already left.
I'm going home.

173
00:19:25,520 --> 00:19:26,880
Uh…

174
00:19:27,400 --> 00:19:28,360
Then I'll drive you.

175
00:19:28,440 --> 00:19:29,720
No, thank you.

176
00:19:29,800 --> 00:19:32,440
I'm going home too. Let me drive you.

177
00:19:47,720 --> 00:19:49,160
Where did she go?

178
00:19:50,640 --> 00:19:52,520
Hathaya, wait for me.

179
00:19:52,600 --> 00:19:54,800
Wait!

180
00:19:55,440 --> 00:19:56,880
Are you okay?

181
00:19:57,880 --> 00:19:58,800
Are you hurt?

182
00:19:58,880 --> 00:20:00,720
No. I'm fine.

183
00:20:00,800 --> 00:20:02,400
I just didn't see the uneven ground.

184
00:20:11,960 --> 00:20:13,440
Careful.

185
00:20:14,200 --> 00:20:18,920
I fell and twisted my ankle.
Raiwin came over to help me.

186
00:20:19,840 --> 00:20:21,160
You don't have to explain.

187
00:20:25,560 --> 00:20:27,240
I'm not jealous of my own brother.

188
00:20:27,760 --> 00:20:29,960
Raiwin is a kind, helpful person.

189
00:20:30,640 --> 00:20:32,040
He likes helping other people.

190
00:20:32,640 --> 00:20:33,600
Right?

191
00:20:34,720 --> 00:20:35,640
Come on.

192
00:20:35,720 --> 00:20:38,800
Let's go home. We need to talk.

193
00:20:50,640 --> 00:20:52,480
Tea, Father.

194
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:55,440
This tea helps lower blood pressure

195
00:20:55,520 --> 00:20:58,760
and cholesterol.

196
00:20:58,840 --> 00:21:02,480
I bought it especially for your health.

197
00:21:03,240 --> 00:21:04,240
Thank you.

198
00:21:08,360 --> 00:21:09,640
Chayanee, where have you been?

199
00:21:09,720 --> 00:21:12,880
I bought Grandpa's favorite sweets.

200
00:21:13,400 --> 00:21:15,440
Aunt Chamoi, please put them on a plate.

201
00:21:15,520 --> 00:21:17,480
Wait. Leave them for now.

202
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:21,440
I just had tea and some snacks
your mother brought me.

203
00:21:24,680 --> 00:21:26,480
Grandpa,

204
00:21:26,560 --> 00:21:30,600
you must be exhausted after working
all week. Let me give you a massage.

205
00:21:34,480 --> 00:21:37,040
You brought my favorite sweets

206
00:21:37,840 --> 00:21:40,000
and now you're giving me a massage.

207
00:21:41,640 --> 00:21:43,080
What do you want this time?

208
00:21:44,840 --> 00:21:48,200
You make it sound like I'm only
being nice because I want something.

209
00:21:49,040 --> 00:21:49,920
Isn't that true?

210
00:21:51,080 --> 00:21:53,080
I hate it when you see right through me.

211
00:21:55,640 --> 00:22:00,360
Grandpa, I want to invest
in a business with a friend.

212
00:22:01,080 --> 00:22:02,360
What kind of business?

213
00:22:02,440 --> 00:22:05,120
Online businesses are booming right now.

214
00:22:05,200 --> 00:22:10,200
My friend owns a skincare factory.
She even asked me to be the presenter.

215
00:22:14,600 --> 00:22:17,200
Our development is already doing well.

216
00:22:18,080 --> 00:22:20,360
Wouldn't it be safer not to risk
another investment?

217
00:22:21,680 --> 00:22:23,760
But Grandpa.

218
00:22:24,840 --> 00:22:28,000
I want to use
my own knowledge and abilities.

219
00:22:28,080 --> 00:22:32,440
Could you give me the chance
to do something on my own?

220
00:22:33,280 --> 00:22:36,360
I'd like ten million baht
as investment capital.

221
00:22:40,840 --> 00:22:42,680
If you're genuinely serious about it,

222
00:22:43,520 --> 00:22:45,640
bring me the business plan,

223
00:22:46,160 --> 00:22:48,360
then I'll consider it.

224
00:22:50,320 --> 00:22:52,160
I already prepared it.

225
00:22:54,840 --> 00:22:57,320
Here's the plan…

226
00:22:59,040 --> 00:23:00,600
for my skincare business, Grandpa.

227
00:23:10,520 --> 00:23:11,480
Put them away.

228
00:23:18,160 --> 00:23:19,120
Chamoi,

229
00:23:19,640 --> 00:23:23,920
put the sweets away.
Bring them out for Father this afternoon.

230
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:24,960
Yes.

231
00:23:28,400 --> 00:23:31,280
Go already.

232
00:23:32,760 --> 00:23:36,600
Madam. Aren't you suspicious?
Not even a little?

233
00:23:37,360 --> 00:23:39,480
Suspicious about what?
What are you trying to say?

234
00:23:39,560 --> 00:23:40,960
Well…

235
00:23:41,640 --> 00:23:43,840
It's Miss Chayanee.

236
00:23:43,920 --> 00:23:48,480
I've never seen her interested
in investing in anything before.

237
00:23:51,160 --> 00:23:52,160
That's true.

238
00:23:52,240 --> 00:23:55,760
I'm surprised too. Normally,
Chayanee talks to me about everything

239
00:23:55,840 --> 00:23:57,720
before she does it.

240
00:24:03,160 --> 00:24:05,720
What? You scared me.

241
00:24:06,320 --> 00:24:08,440
Madam. What if…

242
00:24:08,520 --> 00:24:09,760
What?

243
00:24:09,840 --> 00:24:14,280
…she's got a man and she's planning
to spend the money on him?

244
00:24:14,360 --> 00:24:15,240
What?

245
00:24:16,280 --> 00:24:17,920
You idiot!

246
00:24:18,000 --> 00:24:19,120
Are you crazy?

247
00:24:19,200 --> 00:24:22,560
My daughter isn't the type to go
throwing money at male hosts.

248
00:24:22,640 --> 00:24:25,920
Chayanee is still dating Raiwin.

249
00:24:27,280 --> 00:24:30,360
That's exactly who I mean, madam.

250
00:24:30,440 --> 00:24:34,240
Raiwin's family isn't exactly

251
00:24:34,320 --> 00:24:36,360
rolling in money.

252
00:24:37,240 --> 00:24:40,600
And he's about to enter politics too.

253
00:24:42,080 --> 00:24:45,280
You know, you might be right.

254
00:24:46,080 --> 00:24:49,640
When Chayanee loves someone,
she goes all in.

255
00:24:51,760 --> 00:24:54,480
Whatever she has, she gives everything.

256
00:24:56,120 --> 00:24:58,520
Exactly, madam. If she has a hundred,
she gives a hundred.

257
00:24:58,600 --> 00:25:00,640
If she has a million,
she spends the whole million.

258
00:25:03,440 --> 00:25:05,920
Go. You talk too much.

259
00:25:06,600 --> 00:25:07,440
But Madam…

260
00:25:07,520 --> 00:25:09,080
Go.

261
00:25:19,080 --> 00:25:23,320
Why did you lie to me
about having a wife and a child?

262
00:25:26,320 --> 00:25:29,600
I didn't lie. I just didn't tell you.

263
00:25:31,760 --> 00:25:33,480
How is that any different?

264
00:25:34,880 --> 00:25:38,840
I didn't tell you because
I didn't think it was necessary.

265
00:25:39,440 --> 00:25:41,160
Then what's the real story?

266
00:25:41,800 --> 00:25:44,200
I'll tell you later.

267
00:25:45,600 --> 00:25:46,760
But right now,

268
00:25:47,360 --> 00:25:48,600
I need your help.

269
00:25:49,440 --> 00:25:50,560
With what?

270
00:25:51,160 --> 00:25:54,800
Nuchwara has business out of town.
Papang is going to stay here for a while.

271
00:25:55,640 --> 00:25:56,960
So?

272
00:25:57,840 --> 00:25:59,640
I need you to help me look after Papang.

273
00:26:01,800 --> 00:26:02,840
Hey.

274
00:26:03,680 --> 00:26:08,240
I didn't come here to be a maid,
and I didn't come here to babysit either.

275
00:26:14,640 --> 00:26:15,960
I'm asking you.

276
00:26:17,520 --> 00:26:18,360
Please help me.

277
00:26:27,040 --> 00:26:29,960
I'll try to do what I can.

278
00:26:34,160 --> 00:26:36,920
You can do it. You love kids.

279
00:26:39,200 --> 00:26:42,480
But remember,
you absolutely cannot tell Papang

280
00:26:43,200 --> 00:26:44,400
why you're staying here.

281
00:26:47,360 --> 00:26:49,040
The two of us

282
00:26:50,000 --> 00:26:51,080
aren't husband and wife.

283
00:26:56,720 --> 00:26:59,680
The fact that everyone
wrongly believes we slept together

284
00:27:00,200 --> 00:27:02,840
is the most embarrassing thing
that has ever happened to me.

285
00:27:03,760 --> 00:27:05,040
I would never tell him.

286
00:27:22,320 --> 00:27:23,840
Papang.

287
00:27:24,360 --> 00:27:26,480
Daddy's back!

288
00:27:26,560 --> 00:27:28,200
Where have you been, Daddy?

289
00:27:28,720 --> 00:27:31,840
Daddy took…

290
00:27:31,920 --> 00:27:34,080
-Auntie!
-Auntie?

291
00:27:34,160 --> 00:27:35,680
Or should I call you Grandma?

292
00:27:37,360 --> 00:27:40,360
Call me big sister! I'm Hathaya.

293
00:27:40,440 --> 00:27:41,720
-Auntie.
-Big sister.

294
00:27:41,800 --> 00:27:44,360
-Auntie.
-Fine. Auntie it is.

295
00:27:46,600 --> 00:27:49,320
Daddy, why did you bring Auntie back?

296
00:27:49,400 --> 00:27:53,520
Well, Mommy left you here with me, right?

297
00:27:53,600 --> 00:27:55,880
So I had to bring

298
00:27:55,960 --> 00:27:58,360
Auntie back to stay with us too.

299
00:27:58,440 --> 00:28:03,120
Auntie can help clean the house,
cook, and most importantly,

300
00:28:03,200 --> 00:28:05,240
help me take care of you.

301
00:28:05,840 --> 00:28:07,720
Are you hungry, Papang?

302
00:28:07,800 --> 00:28:10,160
I'm hungry, Daddy.

303
00:28:10,240 --> 00:28:13,440
Then what would you like to eat?
Auntie will make it for you.

304
00:28:13,520 --> 00:28:16,280
I want fried chicken, Daddy.

305
00:28:16,880 --> 00:28:20,160
Okay. Then Auntie will make you some.

306
00:28:20,240 --> 00:28:22,040
I don't want it. It won't taste good.

307
00:28:23,120 --> 00:28:27,920
Daddy, can you order some for me? Please?

308
00:28:28,480 --> 00:28:29,720
Please?

309
00:28:44,160 --> 00:28:46,280
-Please…
-Of course.

310
00:28:46,360 --> 00:28:49,560
My son. I'll order some.

311
00:28:49,640 --> 00:28:52,560
Fried chicken, right?

312
00:28:53,320 --> 00:28:55,080
Come on.

313
00:28:55,160 --> 00:28:56,800
How many pieces do you want?

314
00:28:58,640 --> 00:29:00,160
Is it good?

315
00:29:01,040 --> 00:29:02,960
Yes, Daddy.

316
00:29:03,040 --> 00:29:04,960
Then eat plenty.

317
00:29:05,760 --> 00:29:06,640
Finish it all.

318
00:29:12,280 --> 00:29:13,560
That's mine.

319
00:29:13,640 --> 00:29:15,720
Papang, you've already had two pieces.

320
00:29:15,800 --> 00:29:19,600
Eating too much isn't good.
There are a lot of carbs and oil.

321
00:29:20,200 --> 00:29:23,360
Daddy, I'm hungry.

322
00:29:24,320 --> 00:29:27,520
Then Auntie can peel some fruit for you.
Or would you like some grapes?

323
00:29:27,600 --> 00:29:30,720
Daddy, I'm hungry.

324
00:29:33,720 --> 00:29:37,240
If you're hungry, you can have mine.

325
00:29:37,320 --> 00:29:38,720
Here.

326
00:29:43,520 --> 00:29:46,960
Then, when you're finished eating,
let's wash the dishes together.

327
00:29:52,400 --> 00:29:58,000
Okay. After we finish eating,
let's make washing dishes into a game.

328
00:29:58,080 --> 00:29:59,880
I'm full. I'm going to play games now.

329
00:30:09,600 --> 00:30:11,200
I will

330
00:30:11,720 --> 00:30:13,440
wash the dishes.

331
00:30:13,520 --> 00:30:15,280
I'll do it.

332
00:30:15,360 --> 00:30:16,480
Go ahead and eat.

333
00:30:22,680 --> 00:30:25,320
You can't keep doing this.

334
00:30:25,400 --> 00:30:30,280
You spoil your son.
Keep this up, and he'll learn nothing.

335
00:30:30,360 --> 00:30:32,160
You're exaggerating.

336
00:30:32,680 --> 00:30:36,240
Papang is still young.
He can change when he gets older.

337
00:30:36,320 --> 00:30:40,240
He's not that little anymore.
You need to teach him now.

338
00:30:40,320 --> 00:30:42,760
Teach him to see household chores
as something normal,

339
00:30:42,840 --> 00:30:45,680
just like playing games,
then he can learn to enjoy them too.

340
00:30:46,520 --> 00:30:48,120
You really like to nag.

341
00:30:48,200 --> 00:30:51,920
I'm serious. Ever since your son got here,

342
00:30:52,000 --> 00:30:55,960
all he does is play games. I watched
a video on game addiction in kids.

343
00:30:56,040 --> 00:30:57,720
It can be really harmful.

344
00:30:59,000 --> 00:30:59,840
But…

345
00:31:01,200 --> 00:31:03,480
I don't want to upset Papang.

346
00:31:03,560 --> 00:31:06,200
I'm afraid he'll become a troubled kid.

347
00:31:06,800 --> 00:31:09,320
But raising him this way will mess him up.

348
00:31:10,720 --> 00:31:12,840
Then what am I supposed to do?

349
00:31:13,920 --> 00:31:14,880
Help me.

350
00:31:33,360 --> 00:31:36,880
You have to control his screen time.
Don't let him play games all day.

351
00:31:51,680 --> 00:31:55,280
-Papang.
-Yes, Daddy?

352
00:31:56,840 --> 00:32:00,280
It's getting late. Let's go to bed.

353
00:32:00,360 --> 00:32:04,160
Just a minute. I'm playing.

354
00:32:15,440 --> 00:32:18,440
But you have been playing all day.

355
00:32:18,520 --> 00:32:20,560
I think your eyes
are probably tired by now.

356
00:32:20,640 --> 00:32:22,880
My eyes aren't tired.

357
00:32:24,040 --> 00:32:25,280
No?

358
00:32:37,400 --> 00:32:42,480
But you said you missed me
and wanted to spend time with me.

359
00:32:42,560 --> 00:32:44,440
You're not paying
any attention to me at all.

360
00:32:44,520 --> 00:32:48,320
I missed you more than anything, Daddy.

361
00:32:49,120 --> 00:32:51,600
Then I'm taking this now. Let's go to bed.

362
00:32:55,440 --> 00:32:56,280
Not working.

363
00:33:08,080 --> 00:33:09,200
Do you love me a lot?

364
00:33:09,280 --> 00:33:12,240
I love you more than anyone, Daddy.

365
00:33:12,320 --> 00:33:14,720
Then you have to go to bed with me. Okay?

366
00:33:14,800 --> 00:33:15,960
Okay.

367
00:33:16,040 --> 00:33:18,720
Then let's turn it off.

368
00:33:20,240 --> 00:33:23,120
Come on. Daddy will fly you upstairs.

369
00:33:23,200 --> 00:33:24,880
Let's fly.

370
00:33:32,360 --> 00:33:35,160
Woo!

371
00:33:41,320 --> 00:33:44,520
Chayanee. It's me.

372
00:33:45,040 --> 00:33:46,920
I'm coming in.

373
00:33:47,440 --> 00:33:50,240
Come in, Mom. The door isn't locked.

374
00:33:57,800 --> 00:33:59,920
What are you doing, sweetheart?

375
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:03,440
I brought you some
hot soy milk before bed.

376
00:34:04,480 --> 00:34:05,480
Just leave it there.

377
00:34:07,000 --> 00:34:08,880
You're putting on cream

378
00:34:08,960 --> 00:34:12,920
and getting ready
to be the presenter, but…

379
00:34:13,000 --> 00:34:17,800
which cream belongs to your friend's
company? I want to try some too.

380
00:34:19,280 --> 00:34:21,800
Mom, do you really want
to know about the cream?

381
00:34:22,320 --> 00:34:24,320
Or do you want to know the truth?

382
00:34:26,159 --> 00:34:28,840
What truth? Nothing at all.

383
00:34:30,199 --> 00:34:34,880
The truth about whether I'm really
going into business with my friend

384
00:34:35,400 --> 00:34:37,639
or whether I made the whole thing up.

385
00:34:37,719 --> 00:34:41,080
Madam! See? Miss Chayanee caught us.

386
00:34:41,600 --> 00:34:42,679
Oops.

387
00:34:45,120 --> 00:34:45,960
Hey.

388
00:34:47,800 --> 00:34:51,520
So you didn't ask Grandpa
for money to invest with your friend?

389
00:34:52,280 --> 00:34:54,120
Then where did you get the business plan?

390
00:34:54,719 --> 00:34:59,320
I borrowed the real business plan
from my friend.

391
00:35:00,720 --> 00:35:03,080
Then what are you going
to do with ten million baht?

392
00:35:03,160 --> 00:35:07,920
I'm giving it to Raiwin
for his election campaign.

393
00:35:10,000 --> 00:35:12,480
I knew it! Why can't I
predict the lottery like this?

394
00:35:12,560 --> 00:35:15,360
This is outrageous!

395
00:35:16,080 --> 00:35:18,320
-Chamoi, leave us.
-Yes.

396
00:35:18,400 --> 00:35:20,840
-Leave that there.
-Yes, yes, yes.

397
00:35:22,280 --> 00:35:25,120
Chayanee, I don't understand.

398
00:35:25,200 --> 00:35:27,400
Why do you have to find money to help him?

399
00:35:28,560 --> 00:35:32,840
Sweetheart, you can't buy love with money.

400
00:35:35,520 --> 00:35:36,880
Uncle Saksit

401
00:35:37,400 --> 00:35:39,760
ordered Raiwin to break up with me.

402
00:35:39,840 --> 00:35:41,760
You have to stop seeing Chayanee.

403
00:35:42,920 --> 00:35:45,480
I won't let anyone look down on me.

404
00:35:46,400 --> 00:35:48,840
I'm going to use money
to slap them in the face.

405
00:35:48,920 --> 00:35:52,280
I'll make them see that
I'm worth more than Hathaya.

406
00:35:55,920 --> 00:35:58,000
But you made this whole story up.

407
00:35:59,360 --> 00:36:01,360
What if Grandpa finds out?

408
00:36:03,320 --> 00:36:05,320
Don't worry about that.

409
00:36:05,880 --> 00:36:07,800
I know how to sweet-talk Grandpa.

410
00:36:07,880 --> 00:36:11,200
Now we just have to wait and see
whether he'll give me the money.

411
00:36:54,120 --> 00:36:55,400
Daddy.

412
00:36:55,480 --> 00:36:56,720
Yes?

413
00:36:57,360 --> 00:36:59,600
Did you order this for me?

414
00:37:00,600 --> 00:37:01,920
No. I didn't order it.

415
00:37:10,800 --> 00:37:13,880
It's delicious. You are such a good cook.

416
00:37:17,080 --> 00:37:21,200
I made the food.

417
00:37:21,280 --> 00:37:24,080
That's right. Aunt Hathaya
made it herself.

418
00:37:24,160 --> 00:37:25,520
It's good, isn't it?

419
00:37:25,600 --> 00:37:28,520
I don't want to eat anymore.

420
00:37:28,600 --> 00:37:32,080
Daddy, can you take me to eat at the mall?

421
00:37:37,480 --> 00:37:40,480
I have urgent work today.

422
00:37:40,560 --> 00:37:42,920
I have to leave soon.

423
00:37:44,040 --> 00:37:46,840
I'll come back later
and take you out to eat.

424
00:37:48,440 --> 00:37:50,720
Please look after Papang for me.

425
00:37:51,280 --> 00:37:55,120
Sure. I'll take very good care of him.

426
00:38:04,440 --> 00:38:05,520
I'm going now.

427
00:38:09,040 --> 00:38:10,880
Daddy, I want to go too.

428
00:38:12,600 --> 00:38:13,520
Uh…

429
00:38:14,400 --> 00:38:15,960
Daddy has to work.

430
00:38:16,040 --> 00:38:18,280
Stay with Aunt Hathaya for now.

431
00:38:18,880 --> 00:38:20,920
I don't want to stay
with the witch auntie.

432
00:38:21,000 --> 00:38:23,160
Aunt Hathaya isn't a witch.

433
00:38:23,240 --> 00:38:25,960
She's actually very kind.

434
00:38:26,040 --> 00:38:30,520
Daddy, please take me with you.
I promise not to be naughty.

435
00:38:32,120 --> 00:38:33,760
Please.

436
00:38:34,600 --> 00:38:35,640
Please.

437
00:38:35,720 --> 00:38:38,040
I love you, Daddy.

438
00:38:39,600 --> 00:38:41,280
Come on. Let's go to work.

439
00:38:42,360 --> 00:38:44,120
Go to work.

440
00:38:44,200 --> 00:38:45,720
I'll take care of Papang.

441
00:38:45,800 --> 00:38:47,040
Daddy.

442
00:38:47,120 --> 00:38:48,400
-But…
-Daddy.

443
00:38:48,480 --> 00:38:49,680
Go to work.

444
00:38:49,760 --> 00:38:52,640
Daddy needs to work so he can
earn money to buy you snacks.

445
00:38:52,720 --> 00:38:54,080
-But…
-I'll go with you.

446
00:38:54,160 --> 00:38:56,000
Go to work. Drive safely.

447
00:38:56,080 --> 00:38:58,520
-Work hard.
-Can I?

448
00:38:59,280 --> 00:39:01,320
Come here. Stay with Auntie.

449
00:39:01,400 --> 00:39:04,400
Let me go with you.

450
00:39:05,160 --> 00:39:06,200
Please…

451
00:39:07,880 --> 00:39:09,480
Daddy.

452
00:39:10,520 --> 00:39:11,360
I'm sorry.

453
00:39:15,280 --> 00:39:17,320
Daddy, come back!

454
00:39:23,160 --> 00:39:26,160
Wait. Listen.

455
00:39:26,240 --> 00:39:27,600
Listen.

456
00:39:27,680 --> 00:39:31,480
Do you hear that? Listen. That's the car.

457
00:39:31,560 --> 00:39:33,280
The car is moving.

458
00:39:34,040 --> 00:39:36,800
And now it's gone. That means

459
00:39:37,880 --> 00:39:41,320
Daddy isn't here anymore.

460
00:39:44,080 --> 00:39:45,480
You witch!

461
00:39:48,120 --> 00:39:50,280
You really want me to be a witch, huh?

462
00:39:50,360 --> 00:39:54,320
Fine. Then I'll turn
a naughty boy into a toad.

463
00:39:54,400 --> 00:39:57,720
No, toads aren't very nice.
How about a lizard?

464
00:39:59,080 --> 00:40:02,280
But they make an annoying noise.
No, not a lizard.

465
00:40:02,360 --> 00:40:05,320
Then a mosquito. A mosquito sounds better.

466
00:40:05,400 --> 00:40:07,440
Right? And once
I turn you into a mosquito,

467
00:40:07,520 --> 00:40:10,520
I'll get a mosquito swatter
and smack you dead.

468
00:40:11,600 --> 00:40:12,440
Scared?

469
00:40:13,440 --> 00:40:14,480
You're scared, aren't you?

470
00:40:15,280 --> 00:40:18,640
If you don't want to become
a mosquito, go eat your food.

471
00:40:18,720 --> 00:40:19,800
No.

472
00:40:20,560 --> 00:40:21,880
-One.
-No.

473
00:40:21,960 --> 00:40:22,960
Two.

474
00:40:31,960 --> 00:40:33,400
Am I going to survive today?

475
00:40:38,320 --> 00:40:40,040
Has Chayanee called yet?

476
00:40:43,080 --> 00:40:44,440
Not yet, Dad.

477
00:40:47,760 --> 00:40:49,280
Then call her.

478
00:40:50,920 --> 00:40:53,640
I already did. She didn't answer.

479
00:40:56,000 --> 00:40:57,360
What's going on with her?

480
00:40:58,800 --> 00:41:01,400
Or has she not gotten
the money from Mr. Pichai yet,

481
00:41:02,760 --> 00:41:04,520
so she's avoiding your calls?

482
00:41:06,240 --> 00:41:08,000
Chayanee loves me very much.

483
00:41:08,680 --> 00:41:11,320
She'll definitely get the money
for us, Dad.

484
00:41:17,120 --> 00:41:18,880
Mr. Pichai is coming downstairs.

485
00:41:21,000 --> 00:41:22,760
Grandpa. Good morning.

486
00:41:22,840 --> 00:41:24,000
Good morning.

487
00:41:24,080 --> 00:41:27,440
Father, did you sleep well?

488
00:41:28,160 --> 00:41:31,080
By the time I finished reading
the business plan, it was very late.

489
00:41:31,600 --> 00:41:33,760
I'm sorry, Grandpa.

490
00:41:33,840 --> 00:41:38,280
I didn't mean to keep you from resting.
You could've read it another day.

491
00:41:40,360 --> 00:41:42,160
If you want to do business,

492
00:41:42,920 --> 00:41:45,160
you can't keep putting things off.

493
00:41:45,840 --> 00:41:47,400
When an opportunity comes,

494
00:41:47,480 --> 00:41:50,400
you have to seize it immediately.

495
00:41:51,520 --> 00:41:55,440
Father, that sounds like you're going
to invest in Chayanee's business.

496
00:41:58,280 --> 00:42:02,120
Thank you, Grandpa.
I love you more than anyone.

497
00:42:07,240 --> 00:42:11,960
I wish your business
prosperity and success.

498
00:42:12,040 --> 00:42:14,160
May you become very wealthy.

499
00:42:15,480 --> 00:42:16,840
Thank you, Grandpa.

500
00:42:17,360 --> 00:42:21,960
I promise I won't disappoint you.

501
00:42:23,960 --> 00:42:28,760
Now that Grandpa gave you the investment,
hurry and sign the deal with your friend.

502
00:42:28,840 --> 00:42:31,800
Yes, Mom. Goodbye, Grandpa.

503
00:42:39,240 --> 00:42:43,320
Raiwin called me several times. I'm going
to take the check to him right away.

504
00:42:43,400 --> 00:42:44,600
Hurry, sweetheart.

505
00:42:44,680 --> 00:42:45,800
Yes.

506
00:42:45,880 --> 00:42:48,760
You should hurry
before Mr. Pichai changes his mind.

507
00:42:49,440 --> 00:42:50,920
You always have to jinx it.

508
00:42:51,000 --> 00:42:52,960
Raiwin is calling you?

509
00:42:53,880 --> 00:42:55,640
No, Mom. It's my friend.

510
00:42:55,720 --> 00:42:58,520
The one whose
business plan I gave Grandpa.

511
00:43:01,240 --> 00:43:02,400
What is it?

512
00:43:04,040 --> 00:43:07,320
My grandpa called you? And?

513
00:43:09,200 --> 00:43:10,840
You told him the truth?

514
00:43:10,920 --> 00:43:14,680
I told you not to say anything to Grandpa.

515
00:43:14,760 --> 00:43:16,400
Don't be angry with your friend.

516
00:43:17,920 --> 00:43:18,920
She's a good person.

517
00:43:20,080 --> 00:43:24,480
She didn't want to lie to me or hurt me.

518
00:43:26,680 --> 00:43:31,840
Father, if you already knew the truth,
why did you still give Chayanee the money?

519
00:43:33,640 --> 00:43:36,520
I wanted to know the price of trust.

520
00:43:40,400 --> 00:43:44,640
I used to think that the love and trust
my granddaughter had for me

521
00:43:46,120 --> 00:43:48,640
were priceless.

522
00:43:50,440 --> 00:43:52,000
But today I learned

523
00:43:53,040 --> 00:43:55,200
they're worth only ten million baht.

524
00:43:57,960 --> 00:43:59,360
Father.

525
00:43:59,880 --> 00:44:01,960
I'm so sorry.

526
00:44:02,040 --> 00:44:05,000
-We never meant to deceive--
-Enough. Don't say anything else.

527
00:44:05,720 --> 00:44:07,520
I don't want to hear excuses.

528
00:44:08,440 --> 00:44:09,720
Grandpa.

529
00:44:10,240 --> 00:44:13,160
Don't you want to know
what I'm going to use the money for?

530
00:44:13,800 --> 00:44:16,560
Can I trust that you'll tell me the truth?

531
00:44:17,720 --> 00:44:20,400
I'm giving the money to Raiwin
for his election campaign.

532
00:44:22,560 --> 00:44:24,720
Raiwin and I have been
together for a long time,

533
00:44:24,800 --> 00:44:28,600
but Uncle Saksit ordered Raiwin
to date Hathaya instead.

534
00:44:28,680 --> 00:44:32,680
He wanted to ride Hathaya's popularity
and use it to build support among voters.

535
00:44:33,280 --> 00:44:35,920
But then Hathaya ended up
sleeping with Ramil first.

536
00:44:38,160 --> 00:44:40,320
Raiwin and I are back together now.

537
00:44:41,480 --> 00:44:45,600
I want to use this money
to support his political campaign.

538
00:44:46,120 --> 00:44:50,640
If Raiwin becomes Subdistrict Chief,
it'll benefit your business too.

539
00:44:50,720 --> 00:44:53,800
I just want you
to be proud of me for once.

540
00:44:55,480 --> 00:44:58,480
How am I supposed to be proud of you
for lying to me?

541
00:45:00,280 --> 00:45:03,480
Grandpa, I'm sorry.

542
00:45:06,400 --> 00:45:07,720
Father.

543
00:45:10,040 --> 00:45:11,160
Chayanee.

544
00:45:12,080 --> 00:45:15,880
Hurry and return the check to Grandpa.
Then go apologize properly.

545
00:45:17,480 --> 00:45:19,880
He's going to be upset
with me either way, Mom.

546
00:45:20,480 --> 00:45:23,480
I'm going to use this money to show him

547
00:45:23,560 --> 00:45:25,080
that I made the right decision.

548
00:45:29,240 --> 00:45:30,360
Chayanee.

549
00:45:37,120 --> 00:45:38,680
Papang.

550
00:45:38,760 --> 00:45:42,120
You've had your food.
Take your plate over there and wash it.

551
00:45:42,200 --> 00:45:43,560
I won't do it.

552
00:45:43,640 --> 00:45:46,320
Auntie is the maid. Auntie can wash it.

553
00:45:47,080 --> 00:45:49,480
I have plenty of other things to do.

554
00:45:49,560 --> 00:45:51,840
Besides, I didn't eat from that plate.

555
00:45:51,920 --> 00:45:54,600
You did. So you should wash it.

556
00:45:54,680 --> 00:45:58,040
I won't wash it. Daddy and Mommy
never make me do things like that.

557
00:45:59,720 --> 00:46:02,040
I understand.

558
00:46:02,120 --> 00:46:05,600
But Ramil asked me to take care of you.

559
00:46:05,680 --> 00:46:08,840
So I have the right
to teach you too, right?

560
00:46:08,920 --> 00:46:10,440
I won't wash it.

561
00:46:10,520 --> 00:46:14,320
Go wash your plate. Or do you want
the witch to turn you into a mosquito?

562
00:46:20,200 --> 00:46:22,800
The plate is broken.
Now I don't have to wash it.

563
00:46:24,400 --> 00:46:27,160
You are the maid, Auntie,
so you have to clean it up.

564
00:46:28,520 --> 00:46:30,240
I'm going to play games.

565
00:46:44,080 --> 00:46:46,920
Auntie! Give it back. I want to play.

566
00:46:49,160 --> 00:46:51,200
Why did you turn it off?
I was about to win!

567
00:46:51,800 --> 00:46:53,400
You'll get the iPad back

568
00:46:53,480 --> 00:46:56,760
when you apologize to me
and help me clean the house.

569
00:46:56,840 --> 00:46:59,400
-No.
-Stop being stubborn.

570
00:46:59,480 --> 00:47:01,160
I won't stop.
What are you gonna do, hit me?

571
00:47:01,240 --> 00:47:04,760
Go ahead. When Daddy comes home,
I'll tell him to fire you.

572
00:47:04,840 --> 00:47:08,720
And I'll call the police.
Adults go to jail for hitting children.

573
00:47:08,800 --> 00:47:11,640
I'm not going to waste
my energy hitting you.

574
00:47:11,720 --> 00:47:13,760
I will call your dad

575
00:47:13,840 --> 00:47:15,880
and tell him not to come back here.

576
00:47:16,640 --> 00:47:18,440
I'll tell him to stay somewhere else.

577
00:47:18,520 --> 00:47:21,480
And I will go with him. We'll leave
the naughty boy here all alone.

578
00:47:21,560 --> 00:47:23,920
Then he won't have to come home
to a naughty boy anymore.

579
00:47:24,680 --> 00:47:29,160
And I'll call your mom and tell her not
to pick you up, since you won't be here.

580
00:47:34,400 --> 00:47:38,200
I don't want to stay
in this house anymore.

581
00:47:38,280 --> 00:47:42,120
I want Daddy! I want Mommy!

582
00:47:49,840 --> 00:47:51,600
Papang. Papang.

583
00:47:51,680 --> 00:47:55,160
Then you have to be a good boy.
No being stubborn or naughty.

584
00:47:56,920 --> 00:47:59,560
Most importantly,
you have to stop crying too.

585
00:48:07,120 --> 00:48:08,040
Okay?

586
00:48:09,560 --> 00:48:12,840
Are you going to be a good boy now?
Stop crying.

587
00:48:14,000 --> 00:48:16,480
Go wash your face in the bathroom.

588
00:48:16,560 --> 00:48:18,520
Auntie will clean up the broken plate.

589
00:48:19,040 --> 00:48:21,920
Then we'll talk about
what you can help me with.

590
00:48:22,680 --> 00:48:24,960
Okay? Okay.

591
00:48:25,520 --> 00:48:26,560
Go on. Bathroom.

592
00:48:36,960 --> 00:48:41,160
I'm sorry. I didn't want to scare you.

593
00:48:42,000 --> 00:48:43,320
But I had to.

594
00:48:56,840 --> 00:48:58,760
Uncle, here's a ten-million-baht check.

595
00:48:58,840 --> 00:49:02,760
You have to make sure Raiwin
is above Ramil in every way.

596
00:49:02,840 --> 00:49:04,280
What happened?

597
00:49:04,360 --> 00:49:05,920
Papang ran away from home.

598
00:49:06,520 --> 00:49:07,840
Whose child is Papang?

599
00:49:07,920 --> 00:49:10,840
-Papang is the child of--
-Ramil and Nuchwara.

600
00:49:10,920 --> 00:49:12,160
NEXT EPISODE

601
00:49:12,240 --> 00:49:13,600
Get your filthy hands off me!

602
00:49:13,680 --> 00:49:15,320
Have you ever loved your own child?

603
00:49:16,440 --> 00:49:17,640
Watch out.

604
00:49:18,520 --> 00:49:21,280
This is because of you, isn't it?
You put Father up to this investigation.

605
00:49:21,360 --> 00:49:22,920
Are you trying to frame me?

606
00:49:23,000 --> 00:49:26,120
If we can't find that file,
then we'll have to destroy the evidence.

607
00:51:21,760 --> 00:51:23,680
Subtitle translation by: Thanit Puncharoen
